{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be your doctor during this stay. You were admitted because of weight loss and poor appetite. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:35:12",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’ve lost a lot of weight—down to 40 kilograms from 50 just a month ago. I feel full quickly, my mouth tastes strange, and I’ve been nauseous. I can’t keep food or even pills down sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:37:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned you were taking pancreatic enzymes at home to help with eating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:38:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, but they made me more nauseous. I stopped them yesterday because I couldn’t keep them down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:40:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. We’ll hold off on those for now. We’ll check your labs and get Nutrition involved to help figure out what you can tolerate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:41:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m just so weak. I don’t know if it’s from not eating or something else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2181-09-06 22:43:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s very likely from the weight loss and poor intake. We’ll make sure you’re getting enough calories and monitor your strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2181-09-07 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your kidney function is expected for someone on dialysis. Your hemoglobin is a bit low, but stable. We’re watching your electrolytes closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2181-09-07 07:18:22",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my INR okay? I’m on warfarin for blood clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2181-09-07 07:20:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was low—only 1.1. That means your blood isn’t thin enough, which increases clot risk. We’re starting a heparin drip to bridge you until the warfarin kicks in better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2181-09-07 07:22:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize. Could that be why I’ve been feeling off?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2181-09-07 07:24:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might contribute, but your symptoms are more likely from poor nutrition. We’ll keep the heparin going until your INR is above 1.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2181-09-07 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nutrition team met with you. They said you’re doing better with clear Nepro and small, frequent meals. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2181-09-07 10:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the clear version doesn’t make me nauseous. But I worry—getting groceries is hard for me at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2181-09-07 10:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re arranging for elder services to help with grocery assistance after discharge. That should make it easier to keep eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2181-09-07 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would be a big help. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2181-09-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 1.4. Still a bit low, but improving. We’ll keep the heparin going a bit longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2181-09-08 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? Being on both heparin and warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2181-09-08 08:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s standard. Heparin works fast, warfarin takes days. We overlap them to prevent clots during the transition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2181-09-08 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2181-09-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your abdominal pain has improved, and you’re tolerating a regular diet. That’s excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2181-09-08 14:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel like I can eat again. But I’m still tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2181-09-08 14:04:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your body’s recovering. We’ll keep monitoring your labs and strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2181-09-09 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had dialysis yesterday as scheduled. Your potassium was high before—5.4—but came down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2181-09-09 07:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I always worry about that. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2181-09-09 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "High potassium can affect your heart, but dialysis helps remove it. We monitor closely, so you’re safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2181-09-09 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 1.6—within the target range. We’ll stop the heparin drip today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2181-09-09 12:17:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! So I’m protected from clots now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2181-09-09 12:19:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood is thin enough. We’ll keep your warfarin adjusted to stay in that range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2181-09-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your weight is stable at 42 kg. That’s a good sign your intake is sufficient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2181-09-10 08:02:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I was scared I’d keep losing weight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2181-09-10 08:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. The combination of nutrition support and home assistance should help you maintain it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2181-09-10 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your bloodwork. Your liver enzymes are normal, which is good—no sign of active pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2181-09-10 15:02:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the abdominal pain isn’t from that anymore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2181-09-10 15:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it seems resolved. The pain you had was likely from the recent pancreatitis, but it’s healing now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2181-09-11 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure was low when you stood up yesterday—orthostatic. We held your labetalol temporarily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2181-09-11 07:47:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I get dizzy when I stand. Should I stop that medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2181-09-11 07:49:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’ll restart it at a lower dose—100 mg twice daily. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2181-09-11 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2181-09-11 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on lamotrigine for seizures and omeprazole for reflux. Both are important to continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2181-09-11 13:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I haven’t had any double vision lately. I think the dose is okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2181-09-11 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Neurology has you on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. Your condition is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:04:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your warfarin as adjusted—3 mg five times a week, 4 mg twice a week. Get your INR checked at dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:06:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the clear Nepro and small meals. Elder services will contact you about grocery help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:10:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to weigh myself daily, like you said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2181-09-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day—could be fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2181-09-13 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your physical exam today shows you’re strong, alert, and your abdomen is soft and not tender."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2181-09-13 07:32:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2181-09-13 07:34:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we like to hear. We’ll finalize discharge papers today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2181-09-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge summary is ready. You’re going home with a plan to maintain nutrition and anticoagulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2181-09-13 14:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mental health meds—trazodone—I’ll keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2181-09-13 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue as needed for anxiety. We didn’t change any of your psychiatric meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2181-09-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. Any nausea or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2181-09-14 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’m feeling steady. Eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2181-09-14 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll see you at discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2181-09-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your final INR is 1.6—perfect. All your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2181-09-15 09:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2181-09-15 09:04:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: INR check at dialysis, daily weights, and follow up with your providers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2181-09-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge orders are in. You’ll get a copy of your updated med list."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2181-09-15 14:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll review it with my pharmacist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2181-09-15 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. And call us if anything changes—especially weight or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2181-09-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Time to go home. You’ve made great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2181-09-16 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2181-09-16 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2181-09-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2181-09-16 10:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2181-09-16 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Safe travels home. Call if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2181-09-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve confirmed your ride is here. You’re officially discharged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2181-09-16 12:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2181-09-16 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re glad we could help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2181-09-16 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final note: your weight stayed stable, you’re eating well, and your INR is therapeutic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2181-09-16 13:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep working on it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2181-09-16 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming everything is in order before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all set. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Stay well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge complete. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re going home stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:12:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too. I’m looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2181-09-16 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve earned it. Goodbye for now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2181-09-06 22:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2181-09-16 14:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A female patient with end-stage renal disease, systemic lupus erythematosus, and antiphospholipid syndrome was admitted for failure to thrive and significant weight loss following a recent hospitalization for post-ERCP pancreatitis. She reported poor oral intake, early satiety, nausea, and difficulty maintaining nutrition at home. During admission, her oral intake improved with dietary modifications, including a switch to clear Nepro supplements, and calorie counts confirmed adequate intake. Her weight stabilized at 42 kg. A subtherapeutic INR of 1.1 was identified, prompting initiation of a heparin drip to bridge anticoagulation until warfarin achieved a therapeutic INR of 1.6. Orthostatic hypotension led to a temporary hold and subsequent dose reduction of labetalol. She remained on home medications including lamotrigine, omeprazole, and trazodone, with no psychiatric medication changes. Hemodialysis was continued throughout the stay. Discharge planning included warfarin dose adjustment, INR monitoring at dialysis, daily weight checks, and coordination with elder services for grocery assistance. She was discharged home in stable condition with improved nutrition and therapeutic anticoagulation.",
    "problems": [
      "Nutritional marasmus",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Thrombotic microangiopathy",
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Primary hypercoagulable state",
      "Systemic lupus erythematosus",
      "Body Mass Index less than 19, adult",
      "Adult failure to thrive",
      "Bipolar disorder, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Transplanted organ removal status",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Gout, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Unspecified glaucoma",
      "Loss of weight",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Calculus of bile duct without mention of cholecystitis, without mention of obstruction",
      "Orthostatic hypotension"
    ]
  }
}
